# Drive backup / fallback directory

Upload the whole `Wedding` folder to Google Drive (My Drive). It mirrors what the backend creates, so it fills any gap if `setup()` was never run or a sheet got lost.

```
Wedding/
  Sheets/       one CSV per Google Sheet tab (header row = exact backend columns)
  Uploads/      original full-quality guest photos/videos (per-event subfolders are auto-created)
  Gift QR/      put eSewa / Khalti / Fonepay / bank QR images here (file name = label)
  Logs/         activity log spreadsheets (auto)
  Invitations/  generated PDF invitations
  Proofs/       screenshot proofs
  Backups/      put periodic CSV exports from the admin page here
```

## Keep it in sync (run before copying to Drive)
The CSV headers must match `SHEETS` in `apps-script/Code.gs` exactly. Regenerate from the repo root:

```
tools\node-v24.21.0-win-x64\node.exe tools\make-drive-backup.js           # rebuild CSVs (keeps any data rows)
tools\node-v24.21.0-win-x64\node.exe tools\make-drive-backup.js --check   # report drift only
```
This writes all 26 tab CSVs

Columns added recently: `Admins.Duties` (Door/Bar/Gifts/Live); `Gifts.AuditStatus`, `AuditedAt`, `AuditedBy` and `AuditNote`; and `Gifts.Relation`, `Source`, `Phone`, `EventId` and `Anon`, which the backend writes. Settings `freeze.*` and `theme.*FamilyPrimary/Accent`, `theme.friend*` and `theme.preset` were added too.

## Restore a missing tab
1. Open the wedding spreadsheet → `File › Import` → choose `Sheets/<Name>.csv` → **Insert new sheet**.
2. Rename the tab to exactly `<Name>` (e.g. `Guests`).
3. Run `setup()` once in Apps Script — it adds any newer columns without touching data.

## Guest import
Fill `Sheets/Guests.csv` (at least `Name`; useful: `Side, Relation, Family, Tags, Phone, AdmitCount, Groups`), then use **Admin › Guests › Import CSV**.
`Tags` is comma-separated, e.g. `Groom's Family, VIP/Elders`. Leave `InviteCode` blank and click **🔑 Generate missing codes**.

Magic link format: `https://<site>/index.html?c=<InviteCode>` — no password; guests are then nudged to add the app to their home screen around event days.
